WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.343 --> 00:00:03.453
(whooshing)

00:00:03.453 --> 00:00:04.286
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:05.880
Today we're going to talk about the habits

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.643
of successful people.

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:09.234
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:11.427
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:12.908
And as always, guys, as you're listening,

00:00:12.908 --> 00:00:15.279
if you hear something that
really, really resonates with you

00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:16.905
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:16.905 --> 00:00:19.432
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:19.432 --> 00:00:21.349
And also, as you write things down,

00:00:21.349 --> 00:00:25.764
you're much more likely to
keep it in here, as well.

00:00:25.764 --> 00:00:27.068
Enjoy.

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.651
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:43.158
(inspirational music)

00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:45.537
- The power of 21.

00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:47.189
So when I've been telling
you to get that gold,

00:00:47.189 --> 00:00:48.757
to get that dream, and
I'm just been telling you,

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.913
driving and driving and
driving and driving,

00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:53.301
what I've been talking
about is consistency.

00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:55.122
And for some of you, for real, for real,

00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:57.106
you'll never have it, you'll never be it,

00:00:57.106 --> 00:00:59.293
you'll never do it because you
don't have any consistency.

00:00:59.293 --> 00:01:00.926
Listen to me, you are killing me

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:02.459
and you are killing yourself.

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:05.384
You start and you stop
and you start and you stop

00:01:05.384 --> 00:01:07.662
and then you start and
you stop and your goal,

00:01:07.662 --> 00:01:10.055
you got to own a wall, you
got the Bentley on the wall,

00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:11.811
you got the gated community on the wall,

00:01:11.811 --> 00:01:12.890
you got the degree on the wall.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.640
But the problem is you
keep starting and stopping

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.284
and starting and stopping.

00:01:17.284 --> 00:01:18.951
And all I'm asking you to do for me

00:01:18.951 --> 00:01:21.140
is I'm asking for consistency.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.441
Alright, alright, so I'm
talking about the power of 21,

00:01:23.441 --> 00:01:24.408
do you hear what I'm telling you?

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:27.280
I'm talking about doing
something for 21 straight days.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.957
Now, it may not work.

00:01:28.957 --> 00:01:30.016
I remember when I first did this.

00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:31.993
The first thing I started,
my boy Holler and Heal,

00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:33.754
he gave me a book called Book of Proverbs

00:01:33.754 --> 00:01:36.274
and he told me to read like
a book of proverbs a day

00:01:36.274 --> 00:01:37.200
for 21 days.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.029
He like, "E, just start a habit!"

00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:41.082
for real, we started
with reading proverbs,

00:01:41.082 --> 00:01:42.556
something real simple, but he said,

00:01:42.556 --> 00:01:45.380
"E, if you can do something for 21 days,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.927
"like you'll never have
to think about it."

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:48.695
I don't know if you caught
what I told you this morning,

00:01:48.695 --> 00:01:50.503
I woke up at 3 o'clock this morning,

00:01:50.503 --> 00:01:52.950
3 o'clock burnt out, tired, like you know,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.250
E, I can't do it.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.676
I just boom went back to sleep,

00:01:55.676 --> 00:01:57.581
boom three minutes later,
my body woke me up.

00:01:57.581 --> 00:01:58.755
What am I saying to you?

00:01:58.755 --> 00:02:00.826
I'm telling you consistency, habits.

00:02:00.826 --> 00:02:02.752
My body like, "Yo E, I don't
know what you're doing.

00:02:02.752 --> 00:02:03.987
"I don't know what you think you're doing,

00:02:03.987 --> 00:02:05.125
"but we don't do that.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.713
"Sleeping's for suckers, get up."

00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:09.870
Listen to me, not my
mind, my body kicked in

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:10.900
and said, "Get up!"

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.361
We're talking about consistency.

00:02:12.361 --> 00:02:15.087
And so I read the Book of
Proverbs 21 straight days, right.

00:02:15.087 --> 00:02:16.548
And I started doing other stuff.

00:02:16.548 --> 00:02:18.260
I said we're going to
exercise for 21 days.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.485
I just started trying
to do stuff for 21 days

00:02:20.485 --> 00:02:22.941
to see if I can do it
and what I discovered is,

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:24.342
for real, and I'm going
to be honest with you all,

00:02:24.342 --> 00:02:26.995
I did 14 days and then I
started all over again.

00:02:26.995 --> 00:02:29.774
This time I did 16 days, then
I started all over again.

00:02:29.774 --> 00:02:31.810
Then I did 18 days and I
started all over again.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.738
And I did 21.

00:02:32.738 --> 00:02:34.700
Some stuff I can do 21 straight days.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.715
Some things I got to start
and stop and start and stop

00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:39.453
and start, but when you get to 21,

00:02:39.453 --> 00:02:41.731
there's power in consistency.

00:02:41.731 --> 00:02:45.564
- What do you see is
some of the common habits

00:02:46.827 --> 00:02:50.145
of these successful people,
outside of believing in the best

00:02:50.145 --> 00:02:52.992
in people like you talked
about, not being as critical,

00:02:52.992 --> 00:02:56.066
you know, being flexible
mentally, whatever.

00:02:56.066 --> 00:02:58.784
What are some of the other habits?

00:02:58.784 --> 00:03:02.367
- I think that the most
important attribute

00:03:03.745 --> 00:03:07.578
of a good leader is
somebody who listens well.

00:03:10.632 --> 00:03:13.549
A good leader knows what he thinks.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.382
So there's no point in
spouting what you think

00:03:19.382 --> 00:03:20.465
to your team.

00:03:22.071 --> 00:03:24.320
What you need to do is
learn from your team,

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.153
learn from your customers, listen.

00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:33.058
I'm a great believer
in writing things down.

00:03:33.058 --> 00:03:34.837
So if I'm having a meeting

00:03:34.837 --> 00:03:38.504
and people are coming
up with lots of ideas,

00:03:40.379 --> 00:03:42.978
if I don't write things down, I
know I'm only going to remember

00:03:42.978 --> 00:03:45.645
a couple of things the next day.

00:03:46.754 --> 00:03:50.238
And often quite a lot of
my meetings are at the bar

00:03:50.238 --> 00:03:52.274
at one in the morning, and
I know definitely I'm not

00:03:52.274 --> 00:03:57.039
going to remember the next day
what my staff have told me.

00:03:57.039 --> 00:03:59.424
So again, write things down.

00:03:59.424 --> 00:04:01.462
And then the next day you
can pull out your list

00:04:01.462 --> 00:04:04.879
and you can set about sorting things out.

00:04:06.121 --> 00:04:09.565
If I'm flying on a Virgin Airline,

00:04:09.565 --> 00:04:12.442
I'll meet all the passengers,
I'll listen to them,

00:04:12.442 --> 00:04:13.682
write things down.

00:04:13.682 --> 00:04:17.667
I'll meet the staff, listen
to them, write things down.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.795
And sometimes it's tiny little things,

00:04:19.795 --> 00:04:22.321
but it's those tiny
little things that make

00:04:22.321 --> 00:04:26.420
for an exceptional company
over an average company.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:30.108
Here in America, Virgin
America, we started it

00:04:30.108 --> 00:04:34.124
a few years ago, I think the
reason it consistently gets

00:04:34.124 --> 00:04:37.642
voted best airline in the
States is because we listen

00:04:37.642 --> 00:04:41.003
and we get all those little details right,

00:04:41.003 --> 00:04:43.670
so that our customers are happy.

00:04:46.069 --> 00:04:49.075
If our customers are happy,
your staff are happy,

00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:50.534
your staff smile.

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:54.658
And it's quite rare in airlines
to have a staff that smile,

00:04:54.658 --> 00:04:56.761
but they do smile because
the customers are happy

00:04:56.761 --> 00:04:57.952
and everybody's happy.

00:04:57.952 --> 00:04:59.946
- So listening is the key.

00:04:59.946 --> 00:05:03.177
- I should mention one
thing about reading.

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:05.742
It was at the library here at Columbia,

00:05:05.742 --> 00:05:09.328
which I spent probably
more time than any other

00:05:09.328 --> 00:05:13.124
student, I lived there, practically.

00:05:13.124 --> 00:05:15.170
And I pulled a book out there,

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.375
happened to be a Who's Who in America,

00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:18.981
and it told me something about
my professor Benjamin Graham

00:05:18.981 --> 00:05:20.849
and then I looked up, and
I went to the librarian

00:05:20.849 --> 00:05:22.571
and I said, "I want to
learn more about this,

00:05:22.571 --> 00:05:24.763
"because I learned this over here."

00:05:24.763 --> 00:05:26.333
That changed my whole life.

00:05:26.333 --> 00:05:30.537
We own Geico now because of that librarian

00:05:30.537 --> 00:05:33.166
directing me to some other book

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.608
and then following through on that.

00:05:34.608 --> 00:05:38.775
It's a chance, I read about
1/5 the pages that Bill does,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.382
but I still spend five,
six hours a day reading.

00:05:43.382 --> 00:05:44.948
You just can learn so much.

00:05:44.948 --> 00:05:46.428
I particularly love biography,

00:05:46.428 --> 00:05:50.095
to be able to live the
lives of these people

00:05:51.509 --> 00:05:54.192
that have been so, seem so extraordinary,

00:05:54.192 --> 00:05:57.157
the lessons and the
excursion that they faced,

00:05:57.157 --> 00:05:58.242
just everything about them.

00:05:58.242 --> 00:06:01.408
You can't get enough of reading.

00:06:01.408 --> 00:06:03.191
- I think my life would be very unbalanced

00:06:03.191 --> 00:06:05.849
by most people's definition,

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:07.932
since I work quite a lot.

00:06:11.124 --> 00:06:12.541
I probably put in

00:06:14.781 --> 00:06:17.586
between 70 and 100 hours a week of work,

00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:18.836
which is a lot.

00:06:25.114 --> 00:06:27.807
And then what most of my
remaining waking hours

00:06:27.807 --> 00:06:29.724
are spent with my kids.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.158
That's my life.

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:35.382
I would say it's roughly unbalanced.

00:06:35.382 --> 00:06:36.811
And then just work like hell.

00:06:36.811 --> 00:06:39.274
I mean you just have to put in, you know,

00:06:39.274 --> 00:06:42.191
80-hour, 100-hour weeks every week.

00:06:44.293 --> 00:06:46.210
- That's a lot of work.

00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:51.465
- But all those things
improve the odds of success.

00:06:51.465 --> 00:06:53.973
If other people are putting
in 40-hour work weeks

00:06:53.973 --> 00:06:56.721
and you're putting in 100-hour work weeks,

00:06:56.721 --> 00:06:59.850
then even if you're doing the same thing,

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.130
you know that in one year you will achieve

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.305
what they achieve,

00:07:04.305 --> 00:07:07.698
you will achieve in four
months what it takes them

00:07:07.698 --> 00:07:09.993
a year to achieve.

00:07:09.993 --> 00:07:13.414
- I'm lucky to know a
lot of famous people,

00:07:13.414 --> 00:07:16.551
Bill Gates, Warren
Buffett, and Jack Welch,

00:07:16.551 --> 00:07:19.942
Larry Page, Mark Zuckerberg,
I know all of them.

00:07:19.942 --> 00:07:22.776
I would like to share with
you that those people,

00:07:22.776 --> 00:07:25.517
the difference between those
people and other people,

00:07:25.517 --> 00:07:28.460
they are always optimistic for the future.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.127
They never complain.

00:07:32.221 --> 00:07:36.607
They always try to solve
the problems of the others.

00:07:36.607 --> 00:07:39.654
And I think, where is the opportunity?

00:07:39.654 --> 00:07:43.483
The opportunity always lies in the place

00:07:43.483 --> 00:07:45.316
where people complain.

00:07:46.402 --> 00:07:48.977
Some people said they
complain, you think, hmm,

00:07:48.977 --> 00:07:53.028
if I can solve that complaint,
that's the opportunity.

00:07:53.028 --> 00:07:54.253
That's what I did.

00:07:54.253 --> 00:07:56.090
Don't complain.

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:57.863
Let the other people complain.

00:07:57.863 --> 00:08:01.542
Those people complain,
those people hold still.

00:08:01.542 --> 00:08:05.679
And do not always say,
"Well, I don't have."

00:08:05.679 --> 00:08:09.133
Think about how you can
make things different.

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:11.720
Use your own brain to think.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.545
- You tried to get into three colleges.

00:08:15.545 --> 00:08:18.071
Each time they rejected you.

00:08:18.071 --> 00:08:21.518
- I tried, there is
examination that young people,

00:08:21.518 --> 00:08:22.650
if you want to go to university,

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:25.000
you have to take the examinations.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.490
So I failed it three times,
but I had a lot of fail.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.321
I failed for funny things.

00:08:29.321 --> 00:08:33.778
I failed a key primary
school test for two times,

00:08:33.778 --> 00:08:37.945
and I failed like three
times for the middle schools.

00:08:41.946 --> 00:08:45.147
You would never believe,
in Hangzhou, my city,

00:08:45.147 --> 00:08:47.730
there is only one middle school

00:08:49.046 --> 00:08:51.743
that last only one year.

00:08:51.743 --> 00:08:54.028
It was changed from primary
school middle school,

00:08:54.028 --> 00:08:56.865
because our graduates of our school,

00:08:56.865 --> 00:09:01.769
no middle school accept us
because we were too bad.

00:09:01.769 --> 00:09:04.436
It would become a middle school.

00:09:06.647 --> 00:09:10.814
- What effect did it have,
though, being rejected?

00:09:11.841 --> 00:09:16.005
- I think we have to get used
to it, we're not that good.

00:09:16.005 --> 00:09:19.273
Even today, we still have
a lot of people reject us.

00:09:19.273 --> 00:09:20.106
I think,

00:09:21.892 --> 00:09:25.548
when I graduate from universities,

00:09:25.548 --> 00:09:29.426
and for three years I tried,
fail in the universities,

00:09:29.426 --> 00:09:33.176
so I applied jobs for
30 times, got rejected.

00:09:34.389 --> 00:09:37.180
I went for a police, they
said, "No, you're not good."

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.097
I went to even the KFC.

00:09:39.957 --> 00:09:43.466
When KFC come to China, come to our city,

00:09:43.466 --> 00:09:45.716
24 people went for the job.

00:09:47.645 --> 00:09:49.462
23 people accepted.

00:09:49.462 --> 00:09:51.958
I was the only other guy.

00:09:51.958 --> 00:09:53.190
And we went for police.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.412
Five people, four of them accepted.

00:09:55.412 --> 00:09:57.918
I was the only guy that
did not receive it.

00:09:57.918 --> 00:10:01.086
So to me, being turned down, rejected,

00:10:01.086 --> 00:10:04.660
oh by the way, I told
you I apply for Harvard

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.342
for 10 times, rejected.

00:10:07.342 --> 00:10:08.635
I know I be rejected, I
just want to say that.

00:10:08.635 --> 00:10:11.718
- [Charlie] They're sorry
now, they're sorry now.

00:10:11.718 --> 00:10:13.163
10 times you wrote them and said,

00:10:13.163 --> 00:10:15.113
"I'd like to come to Harvard."

00:10:15.113 --> 00:10:17.093
- Yeah, and then I told myself some day

00:10:17.093 --> 00:10:19.579
I should go teach there, maybe.

00:10:19.579 --> 00:10:20.802
- Here's what I've created for my life

00:10:20.802 --> 00:10:22.878
and anyone I know succeeding.

00:10:22.878 --> 00:10:26.804
I'm a 17 year-old kid
from Azusa, California,

00:10:26.804 --> 00:10:29.827
with no real education
other than self-education,

00:10:29.827 --> 00:10:32.669
with no background, with
parents that did their best,

00:10:32.669 --> 00:10:33.669
all of them,

00:10:36.363 --> 00:10:38.713
with no money, but I did one thing.

00:10:38.713 --> 00:10:42.178
I love people and I had an enormous demand

00:10:42.178 --> 00:10:44.900
I made upon myself and I sculpted my mind

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.405
and my emotions to get me
to do whatever it would take

00:10:47.405 --> 00:10:49.899
to achieve and to contribute.

00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:52.465
But to do that, I did it by using my body

00:10:52.465 --> 00:10:53.980
and changing my focus.

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:56.717
I did it by putting
myself in a key physiology

00:10:56.717 --> 00:10:59.364
and using what I call incantations.

00:10:59.364 --> 00:11:02.806
Can you train yourself to
believe something, yes or no?

00:11:02.806 --> 00:11:03.893
Absolutely.

00:11:03.893 --> 00:11:05.304
How many of you have ever
made the fatal mistake

00:11:05.304 --> 00:11:07.738
of going to Disneyland or Disney World

00:11:07.738 --> 00:11:09.377
and while you're there
made the fatal mistake

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:14.281
of going to a ride called
It's a Small World After All?

00:11:14.281 --> 00:11:15.933
What happens for about
a week after you're out

00:11:15.933 --> 00:11:17.831
of that damn place?

00:11:17.831 --> 00:11:19.230
You're still singing
this thing in your head

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.633
in 24 languages, right?

00:11:21.633 --> 00:11:22.715
Well let me tell you something.

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:24.914
How many of you have things
when you want to go achieve them

00:11:24.914 --> 00:11:26.292
and then this part of your voice goes,

00:11:26.292 --> 00:11:28.119
"Oh, it's not going to
happen," or "Forget it."

00:11:28.119 --> 00:11:29.614
How many get a voice
that sometimes interrupts

00:11:29.614 --> 00:11:32.410
that good pattern, say "Aye."

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:35.254
What you want to do is train a new one.

00:11:35.254 --> 00:11:38.646
So starting when I was 17, I
started doing incantations,

00:11:38.646 --> 00:11:40.063
not affirmations.

00:11:41.163 --> 00:11:42.663
Affirmation you go, "I'm happy, I'm happy,

00:11:42.663 --> 00:11:44.775
"I'm happy, I'm happy, I'm happy."

00:11:44.775 --> 00:11:45.623
What's the problem?

00:11:45.623 --> 00:11:47.564
You haven't changed your what?

00:11:47.564 --> 00:11:48.397
Your what?

00:11:49.313 --> 00:11:50.873
Physiology, if you don't
change your physiology,

00:11:50.873 --> 00:11:52.195
you won't get anything.

00:11:52.195 --> 00:11:54.830
So in incantations, not
only do you speak it,

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:56.710
but you embody what you're saying

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.095
with all the intensity you can.

00:11:58.095 --> 00:11:59.661
Then you do it with enough repetitions

00:11:59.661 --> 00:12:00.876
that it sticks in your head.

00:12:00.876 --> 00:12:03.056
Like It's a Small World, now
the conversation in your head

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:05.694
is always the same and it
gives you what you want.

00:12:05.694 --> 00:12:08.480
So use your body and your voice.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.821
So, 17 years ago, I started doing things.

00:12:10.821 --> 00:12:13.153
I was working for Jim Rohn, the speaker.

00:12:13.153 --> 00:12:15.619
I was 17 years old, I had long hair,

00:12:15.619 --> 00:12:18.413
minestrone soup acne on my face.

00:12:18.413 --> 00:12:21.231
I was trying to call on
Bear Stearns type of people

00:12:21.231 --> 00:12:22.412
and convince them why they should go

00:12:22.412 --> 00:12:24.451
to this man's seminar
and be more successful.

00:12:24.451 --> 00:12:27.184
I was driving a 1968 Volkswagon

00:12:27.184 --> 00:12:29.802
that I had earned at 40
hours a week as a janitor.

00:12:29.802 --> 00:12:32.712
The only way I did it was
park far from the building

00:12:32.712 --> 00:12:34.658
and then go in, and I love people.

00:12:34.658 --> 00:12:36.559
I believe when I put myself in state,

00:12:36.559 --> 00:12:37.832
and I was able to
influence people that were

00:12:37.832 --> 00:12:40.102
far more successful
that I was at the time.

00:12:40.102 --> 00:12:42.237
I would do something
that I still do backstage

00:12:42.237 --> 00:12:45.080
and I've done for 23 years,

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.974
because I don't hope I'm
going to be in good state,

00:12:46.974 --> 00:12:48.213
I demand it.

00:12:48.213 --> 00:12:50.225
So I do an incantation,
using my whole body,

00:12:50.225 --> 00:12:52.868
and saying, "I now command
my subconscious mind

00:12:52.868 --> 00:12:54.702
"to direct me in helping
as many people as possible

00:12:54.702 --> 00:12:57.067
"alive today to better their lives.

00:12:57.067 --> 00:12:58.851
"Body, give me the strength, the emotion,

00:12:58.851 --> 00:13:00.261
"the persuasion, the humor, the brevity,

00:13:00.261 --> 00:13:02.194
"whatever it takes to show these people

00:13:02.194 --> 00:13:04.441
"and to get these people
to change their lives now."

00:13:04.441 --> 00:13:06.493
And I will do that literally
driving in my Volkswagon

00:13:06.493 --> 00:13:10.319
to a meeting in LA on a
freeway for 40 minutes.

00:13:10.319 --> 00:13:11.152
People are looking at me,

00:13:11.152 --> 00:13:12.723
I'm screaming at the top of my lungs.

00:13:12.723 --> 00:13:16.585
They're going, "I know he's a
serial killer, I know he is."

00:13:16.585 --> 00:13:18.406
But by the time I enter that room,

00:13:18.406 --> 00:13:21.916
when two people meet, if there's rapport,

00:13:21.916 --> 00:13:24.238
the person who's most certain

00:13:24.238 --> 00:13:26.402
will always influence the other person.

00:13:26.402 --> 00:13:28.363
And I was totally certain
and they were trying

00:13:28.363 --> 00:13:30.535
to get revved up to certainty.

00:13:30.535 --> 00:13:32.819
Do you agree with this, yes or no?

00:13:32.819 --> 00:13:34.374
I do another one, because I was poor,

00:13:34.374 --> 00:13:35.330
I changed my mindset.

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:38.114
I kept doing things but
I never got beyond it.

00:13:38.114 --> 00:13:40.184
I'd say, "God's wealth is
circulating in my life.

00:13:40.184 --> 00:13:43.239
"It's what flows to me in
avalanches of abundance.

00:13:43.239 --> 00:13:45.922
"All my needs, desires, and goals are met

00:13:45.922 --> 00:13:48.501
"instantaneously by infinite intelligence,

00:13:48.501 --> 00:13:51.513
"for I am one with God
and God is everything."

00:13:51.513 --> 00:13:52.928
And I would imagine the
abundance in my life

00:13:52.928 --> 00:13:54.871
and I would feel so grateful.

00:13:54.871 --> 00:13:56.867
And a year later I went
from making $38,000 a year

00:13:56.867 --> 00:13:58.815
to making a million
dollars a year in one year.

00:13:58.815 --> 00:14:00.377
- I've started, and I'm still
not great at this, either,

00:14:00.377 --> 00:14:03.139
and these are always works in progress

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:05.611
when it's not the thing that
comes most natural to you.

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:07.467
But what I think I've
been doing well lately

00:14:07.467 --> 00:14:09.660
is I've been giving more honest, critical

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.835
direct to people's face feedback.

00:14:11.835 --> 00:14:13.722
I tend to be a little bit softer.

00:14:13.722 --> 00:14:15.644
I'm much more of a honey over vinegar guy.

00:14:15.644 --> 00:14:19.811
Between our former managing
director Kelly and AJ,

00:14:20.879 --> 00:14:23.228
they're very straight shooter operators,

00:14:23.228 --> 00:14:24.676
they've moved me along.

00:14:24.676 --> 00:14:26.732
I've definitely evolved in that category.

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:28.604
I'm definitely better at it.

00:14:28.604 --> 00:14:32.765
I still want to deal with a ton
of empathy and heart and soul,

00:14:32.765 --> 00:14:36.475
but shooting it straight is
bringing more value to me

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:39.337
and it's just speeding up
the process of victory.

00:14:39.337 --> 00:14:40.696
Can't have a CEO,

00:14:40.696 --> 00:14:41.958
I don't know I wouldn't say I'm not,

00:14:41.958 --> 00:14:44.383
I'm very decisive, but
boy, delivering bad news

00:14:44.383 --> 00:14:46.339
does not come natural to
me and I don't love it.

00:14:46.339 --> 00:14:48.258
So building infrastructure around me

00:14:48.258 --> 00:14:50.466
and then doing it myself
has been important.

00:14:50.466 --> 00:14:52.373
Evolution that I've done been much better

00:14:52.373 --> 00:14:53.815
at being a mediator than
I've done on Wine Library,

00:14:53.815 --> 00:14:55.085
and what that's given me is the thing

00:14:55.085 --> 00:14:56.235
that a lot of you know that I value,

00:14:56.235 --> 00:14:58.206
which is speed, those two.

00:14:58.206 --> 00:14:59.367
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:59.367 --> 00:15:02.433
I made this video because
Imane Injar asked me to.

00:15:02.433 --> 00:15:03.816
If there's a topic you'd like me to cover

00:15:03.816 --> 00:15:05.423
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:15:05.423 --> 00:15:06.953
please leave it down in the comments below

00:15:06.953 --> 00:15:08.184
and I'll see what I can do.

00:15:08.184 --> 00:15:10.429
I'd also love to know what
did you learn from this video?

00:15:10.429 --> 00:15:12.086
What was the most important takeaway

00:15:12.086 --> 00:15:14.120
that you're going to apply to your life

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.029
or your business immediately,
now that you saw this clip?

00:15:17.029 --> 00:15:18.767
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:15:18.767 --> 00:15:20.265
If you have anything you'd like to add,

00:15:20.265 --> 00:15:22.028
a tip, a suggestion for other people

00:15:22.028 --> 00:15:24.772
to be more successful, habits
that you feel maybe we missed,

00:15:24.772 --> 00:15:26.123
leave it down again in the comments.

00:15:26.123 --> 00:15:27.930
I'm really curious to
see what you wave to say.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.383
Finally I want to give a quick
shoutout to Esteben Serrano.

00:15:30.383 --> 00:15:32.208
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:15:32.208 --> 00:15:34.351
Your One Word, it really,
really, really, really

00:15:34.351 --> 00:15:37.405
means a lot to me, and I hope
you're enjoying the read.

00:15:37.405 --> 00:15:38.705
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:15:38.705 --> 00:15:39.815
I believe in you.

00:15:39.815 --> 00:15:41.877
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:15:41.877 --> 00:15:43.561
And whatever your One Word is,

00:15:43.561 --> 00:15:47.922
much love, have an amazing
day, and I'll see you soon.

00:15:47.922 --> 00:15:50.255
(whooshing)

